WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.710
1818.

2
00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:04.340
Night, in a garret workroom.

3
00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:08.580
A young scientist bends over
his bench, among glass jars.

4
00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:12.980
His dream: "Life and death
appeared to me ideal bounds,

5
00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:16.880
which I should first break through," 1897.

6
00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:20.090
A telescope watches a red dot in the sky.

7
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:26.950
And something there is watching back, with
"intellects vast and cool and unsympathetic,"

8
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.090
Two novels, nearly eighty years apart.

9
00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:33.110
So what do these writers
fear science will do?

10
00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:37.330
In this mission, you'll see each novel
answer the science of its own day:

11
00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:40.510
electricity in one,
evolution in the other.

12
00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.610
And you'll meet humans who
discover they are being watched,

13
00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:46.020
like creatures in a drop of water.

14
00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:50.220
Your mission: work out what these
writers fear science will do.
